   CCUUSSTTOOMMIIZZIINNGG TTHHEE SSTTAARRTTUUPP PPRROOCCEEDDUURREE
       Of course, any of the existing files can be edited in place.

       Because  the  order in which the various scripts in _/_e_t_c_/_X_1_1_/_X_s_e_s_s_i_o_n_._d
       are executed is important, files to be added to this  directory  should
       have a well-formed name.  The following format is recommended:

       * a two-digit number denoting sequence;

       *  the  name  of  the package providing the script (or ‘custom’ for lo‐
       cally-created scripts);

       * an underscore;

       * a description of the script's basic function, using  only  characters
       allowed by rruunn--ppaarrttss.

       Here  is  an  example  of  how  one  might write a script, named _4_0_c_u_s_‐
       _t_o_m___l_o_a_d_-_x_m_o_d_m_a_p, to invoke xxmmooddmmaapp(1):

       SYSMODMAP="/etc/X11/Xmodmap"
       USRMODMAP="$HOME/.Xmodmap"

       if [ -x /usr/bin/X11/xmodmap ]; then
           if [ -f "$SYSMODMAP" ]; then
               xmodmap "$SYSMODMAP"
           fi
       fi

       if [ -x /usr/bin/X11/xmodmap ]; then
           if [ -f "$USRMODMAP" ]; then
               xmodmap "$USRMODMAP"
           fi
       fi

