       mmeessssaaggee  is  used for communicating with the user.  It is a wrapper for
       the eecchhoo(1) command and relies upon eecchhoo for its  argument  processing.
       This function may be given an arbitrarily long message string, which is
       formatted to the user's terminal width (breaking lines  at  whitespace)
       and sent to standard error.  If the _D_I_S_P_L_A_Y environment variable is set
       and the xxmmeessssaaggee(1) program is available, xxmmeessssaaggee is also used to dis‐
       play the message.

